  "info": {
    "lines": [
      "See: <a href=\"help.html#runningSongFromLibrary\">Tips for running from the Song Library</a><br>",
      "<br>",
      "<br>",
      "This song is just like <a href=\"?song=name-that-note/name-that-note.json\">name-that-note</a>, but it uses \"placed single note\" as the ArpeggioPlugin type: <cmd-line> /fpat<i> <b>p</b>laced single</i></cmd-line>  By default, it has SingleNotes placed at the Nut, 5th, 7th, and 12th frets, since in P4 this gives the fourth, the fifth, and the octave.  To change the name-that-note excercise to just exact note positions, turn off <b>HIDE Single Notes</b>, then place SingleNotes you want to practice, then turn <b>HIDE Single Notes</b> back on.",
      "<br>",
      "<br>",
      "Default is S6, positions [0,4], and Chromatic Transposition.  Use the links below to set other Tunings, Positions, and Transpositions.",
